3015 - Director, Media Solutions - Scrum Master, UK

Role Summary and Impact &nbsp;

You will work closely with teams across the United States, Europe, and Asia to deliver high-impact solutions in a collaborative, multicultural environment.&nbsp;We are seeking an experienced and passionate Scrum Master to guide and coach our development teams within Data &amp; Technology Solutions. You will be a champion of Agile values and principles, fostering a culture of continuous improvement, transparency, and self-organization. Your role will be critical in enabling our teams to deliver high-quality data products and AI platforms efficiently and effectively, contributing directly to WPP's innovation in the AdTech space.&nbsp;

You are:&nbsp;

• A leader who empowers teams, removing impediments and fostering an environment of collaboration and psychological safety.&nbsp;

• An expert facilitator, skilled at guiding teams through Agile ceremonies and discussions to achieve clear outcomes.&nbsp;

• A strong communicator and coach, adept at nurturing Agile mindsets and practices across individuals and the organization.&nbsp;

• Proactive and adaptable, able to anticipate challenges, resolve conflicts, and guide teams through change.&nbsp;

• Passionate about continuous improvement, always seeking ways to optimize team performance and delivery predictability.&nbsp;

What you will do:

Facilitate Agile Processes and Ceremonies &nbsp;

• Facilitate all Scrum ceremonies (e.g., Daily Scrum, Sprint Planning, Sprint Review, Sprint Retrospective) ensuring they are productive, engaging, and aligned with Agile principles.&nbsp;

• Help the Product Owner manage the product backlog, ensuring stories are well-defined, estimated, and prioritized.&nbsp;

• Support the team in self-organizing and cross-functional collaboration, helping them to achieve sprint goals and ultimately, product vision.&nbsp;

• Ensure transparent communication of team progress, impediments, and metrics to all relevant stakeholders.&nbsp;

Coach and Develop Agile Teams &nbsp;

• Coach the development team on Scrum principles, Agile values, and engineering best practices to maximize productivity and continuous improvement.&nbsp;

• Provide guidance and support to the Product Owner in understanding and implementing Agile practices, particularly regarding backlog management and stakeholder collaboration.&nbsp;

• Foster a culture of open communication, inspect-and-adapt, and continuous learning within the team.&nbsp;

• Help resolve team conflicts and build a strong sense of team ownership and accountability.&nbsp;

Remove Impediments and Protect the Team&nbsp;

• Identify, track, and actively work to remove impediments that hinder the team's progress and productivity.&nbsp;

• Shield the team from external distractions and interferences, allowing them to focus on sprint commitments.&nbsp;

• Collaborate with other Scrum Masters and management to identify and address organizational impediments to Agile adoption.&nbsp;

• Promote effective decision-making processes within the team, encouraging autonomy while ensuring alignment with broader goals.&nbsp;

Drive Continuous Improvement and Metrics&nbsp;

• Guide the team in using metrics (e.g., velocity, burn-down/up charts) to understand and improve their performance and predictability.&nbsp;

